1
00:00:06,214 --> 00:00:09,884
All right, classes are starting!
Back to your classrooms!

2
00:00:09,968 --> 00:00:11,594
Come on, hurry!

3
00:00:11,678 --> 00:00:13,096
Hurry up, come on!

4
00:00:16,349 --> 00:00:18,184
Get back to class!

5
00:00:28,695 --> 00:00:29,821
That hurts!

6
00:00:29,904 --> 00:00:33,491
Hey, everyone, Mr. Shibata hit Sho!

7
00:00:33,575 --> 00:00:34,534
What?!

8
00:00:38,663 --> 00:00:40,206
What's happening?

9
00:00:57,057 --> 00:01:01,227
Habu, I’m really curious about that.
You're always--

10
00:01:01,311 --> 00:01:03,271
Good morning.

11
00:01:04,272 --> 00:01:08,276
Apologies for the delayed greeting.
My name is Aso, and I’m a lawyer.

12
00:01:08,777 --> 00:01:11,780
Good morning, Ms. Aso.
You look lovely today too.

13
00:01:12,739 --> 00:01:13,740
Thank you very much.

14
00:01:13,823 --> 00:01:17,786
-Do you have a boyfriend?
-Shut up. It's nice meeting you too.

15
00:01:17,869 --> 00:01:19,537
I'll introduce you. Follow me.

16
00:01:19,621 --> 00:01:20,789
-Mr. Kureta!
-Yes!

17
00:01:20,872 --> 00:01:22,540
Over there is our director, Mr. Kureta.

18
00:01:22,624 --> 00:01:23,541
Hello there.

19
00:01:23,625 --> 00:01:26,044
Ms. Konno handles
accounting and general tasks.

20
00:01:26,127 --> 00:01:27,295
Nice to meet you.

21
00:01:27,378 --> 00:01:31,049
And I’m Sabayama, a first-class architect,
just like the director.

22
00:01:31,132 --> 00:01:34,177
This is our assistant, Habu.

23
00:01:34,260 --> 00:01:35,428
I’m Kota Habu.

24
00:01:35,512 --> 00:01:38,515
I’m just an assistant,
but I’m better at the job than Sabayama.

25
00:01:38,598 --> 00:01:41,184
Hey, I'm your senior,
call me Mr. Sabayama!

26
00:01:41,267 --> 00:01:44,562
I’m Nakazaki, a part-timer.
I study law at Risshu University.

27
00:01:44,646 --> 00:01:45,855
You study law?

28
00:01:45,939 --> 00:01:50,401
I tried to get a job at the law firm,
but I ended up working here.

29
00:01:51,611 --> 00:01:54,572
Oh, Ms. Aso. Would you like
something to drink? Have a seat.

30
00:01:54,656 --> 00:01:56,491
-No, I'm fine.
-Maybe some coffee?

31
00:01:56,574 --> 00:01:58,368
-I'm fine--
-Excuse me…

32
00:01:59,160 --> 00:02:03,331
Is this Mr. Uramawashi's office?

33
00:02:03,414 --> 00:02:06,918
Oh, yes. But for now, he's suspended…

34
00:02:07,001 --> 00:02:12,465
For the house of Mr. and Mrs. Shimizu,
let's use a tensegrity structure.

35
00:02:13,091 --> 00:02:16,761
The ceiling will look otherworldly.

36
00:02:18,680 --> 00:02:21,558
Excuse me, are you Mr. Uramawashi?

37
00:02:22,267 --> 00:02:23,685
What can I do for you?

38
00:02:24,769 --> 00:02:27,856
Please help my father.

39
00:02:36,156 --> 00:02:39,284
My father teaches at Karasawa Junior High,

40
00:02:39,784 --> 00:02:42,162
and he hit a student.

41
00:02:42,245 --> 00:02:44,289
<i>Hey, everyone, Mr. Shibata hit Sho!</i>

42
00:02:44,372 --> 00:02:47,250
The student's parents
filed a police report,

43
00:02:47,333 --> 00:02:49,252
and my father was arrested.

44
00:02:49,335 --> 00:02:52,255
Do you know why he resorted to violence?

45
00:02:53,715 --> 00:02:57,385
He said he was just warning them
about their messy attire,

46
00:02:58,052 --> 00:03:01,222
but he's not the type of man
to hit someone just for that.

47
00:03:01,306 --> 00:03:03,433
Is there anything else you can think of?

48
00:03:03,516 --> 00:03:06,769
No, he wouldn't tell me anything.

49
00:03:08,354 --> 00:03:12,942
That's when I found Mr. Uramawashi's
business card on my father's desk.

50
00:03:19,657 --> 00:03:21,826
I must save my father!

51
00:03:21,910 --> 00:03:24,787
I'll pay you,
even if it takes my whole life.

52
00:03:24,871 --> 00:03:25,955
Please!

53
00:03:30,168 --> 00:03:33,254
Your love for your father is touching.

54
00:03:33,338 --> 00:03:36,549
However, I'm currently suspended.

55
00:03:36,633 --> 00:03:39,844
If I have any contact with clients,
it would be a violation,

56
00:03:39,928 --> 00:03:42,972
and Ms. Aso here will report me.

57
00:03:43,056 --> 00:03:43,973
No, I--

58
00:03:44,057 --> 00:03:46,726
I’m sorry I can’t be of help.

59
00:03:49,312 --> 00:03:50,480
Understood.

60
00:03:58,821 --> 00:03:59,989
Please wait!

61
00:04:02,283 --> 00:04:05,245
If you don't mind, I can help you.

62
00:04:08,414 --> 00:04:09,832
Thank you very much.

63
00:04:16,965 --> 00:04:20,218
You don't see passionate teachers
like him much nowadays.

64
00:04:20,301 --> 00:04:22,136
Used to be lots of them back in the day.

65
00:04:22,220 --> 00:04:25,139
Mr. Uramawashi,
I am the defense counsel for this case.

66
00:04:25,223 --> 00:04:29,477
I’m just stating my personal opinion.
My view on this is…

67
00:04:29,560 --> 00:04:31,062
That’s quite enough.

68
00:04:31,145 --> 00:04:32,522
Do you dislike me?

69
00:04:33,231 --> 00:04:35,233
It’s not about liking or disliking.

70
00:04:35,900 --> 00:04:39,279
You are currently suspended, right?

71
00:04:39,362 --> 00:04:44,033
Besides, Mr. Uramawashi, you and I have
completely different mindsets as lawyers.

72
00:04:44,117 --> 00:04:45,076
Mindsets?

73
00:04:45,159 --> 00:04:48,037
In my life so far,
I have never told a single lie.

74
00:04:48,121 --> 00:04:49,706
Such a person actually exists?

75
00:04:49,789 --> 00:04:51,958
You're supposed to laugh.

76
00:04:52,041 --> 00:04:53,751
I’m not joking.

77
00:04:53,835 --> 00:04:56,671
It's meaningless
to win something through a lie.

78
00:04:57,213 --> 00:04:59,549
When I’m about to lie, I wait six seconds.

79
00:04:59,632 --> 00:05:02,885
Then the lie starts to feel ridiculous.

80
00:05:02,969 --> 00:05:08,224
-One, two, three, four…
-What?

81
00:05:08,308 --> 00:05:11,144
-What? Wait…
-Five, six.

82
00:05:12,103 --> 00:05:15,523
What a coincidence. I hate lies too.

83
00:05:18,192 --> 00:05:21,029
The effect varies from person to person.

84
00:05:21,779 --> 00:05:24,532
Sometimes a lie is necessary
to unravel another lie.

85
00:05:25,825 --> 00:05:29,537
No, you destroy lies with the truth!

86
00:05:29,620 --> 00:05:32,790
You are like
the Christchurch Cardboard Cathedral.

87
00:05:32,874 --> 00:05:35,251
-Nice one.
-Another architecture reference?

88
00:05:35,335 --> 00:05:37,253
He means you're stronger than you look.

89
00:05:38,504 --> 00:05:39,714
That's enough.

90
00:05:39,797 --> 00:05:42,717
You and I
will never understand each other.

91
00:05:43,301 --> 00:05:44,218
Whoa!

92
00:05:44,844 --> 00:05:47,722
-What's going on?
-Move aside!

93
00:05:49,807 --> 00:05:50,641
Go on!

94
00:05:51,476 --> 00:05:53,603
What is this all of a sudden?

95
00:05:53,686 --> 00:05:56,439
-Aso, record this.
-Huh?

96
00:05:56,522 --> 00:05:57,607
Hurry up.

97
00:05:57,690 --> 00:06:01,569
Huh? Look, this is too sudden…

98
00:06:01,652 --> 00:06:03,362
Hang on… Okay.

99
00:06:03,946 --> 00:06:07,909
No, maybe this angle is better. Wait…

100
00:06:10,912 --> 00:06:12,580
What just came over you?

101
00:06:12,663 --> 00:06:14,499
-Show me.
-Okay.

102
00:06:14,582 --> 00:06:16,375
-I want to see!
-Here.

103
00:06:17,668 --> 00:06:20,004
<i>No, maybe this angle is better.</i>

104
00:06:20,088 --> 00:06:21,380
What do you think?

105
00:06:22,507 --> 00:06:24,008
You two are pretty good.

106
00:06:24,092 --> 00:06:28,221
-Right?
-We were trying to copy Monaki.

107
00:06:28,304 --> 00:06:31,641
-I see.
-That’s not what you should be looking at.

108
00:06:31,724 --> 00:06:33,101
Huh?

109
00:06:33,184 --> 00:06:34,519
Hey, that's…

110
00:06:34,602 --> 00:06:36,270
<i>No, maybe…</i>

111
00:06:36,354 --> 00:06:39,524
At the beginning of the video,
the camera is shaky.

112
00:06:39,607 --> 00:06:43,152
Well, that's because you suddenly
told me to start filming.

113
00:06:43,236 --> 00:06:47,365
Yes, a spontaneous recording
always starts like this.

114
00:06:52,411 --> 00:06:54,997
Wait, excuse me!

115
00:06:55,081 --> 00:06:58,126
FLAMING MONSTER

116
00:06:58,209 --> 00:07:01,712
The video of Mr. Shibata was stable.

117
00:07:01,796 --> 00:07:04,423
Someone set up a camera in advance!

118
00:07:06,050 --> 00:07:07,635
Hey, I have to go!

119
00:07:10,096 --> 00:07:13,516
Hey, don't do anything on your own, okay?

120
00:07:13,599 --> 00:07:15,268
I'll focus on my work.

121
00:07:15,351 --> 00:07:20,815
Right now, you are an architect,
not a lawyer. Got that? An architect!

122
00:07:23,443 --> 00:07:25,069
All right, everyone,

123
00:07:26,154 --> 00:07:28,156
time to expose the lie.

124
00:08:10,573 --> 00:08:12,658
May I ask who you are?

125
00:08:12,742 --> 00:08:16,454
I apologize for the sudden visit.
My name is Aso, and I’m a lawyer.

126
00:08:17,205 --> 00:08:19,290
I have questions
about Mr. Shibata's case--

127
00:08:19,373 --> 00:08:21,042
We have nothing to tell you!

128
00:08:22,168 --> 00:08:26,255
There’s a possibility that the video
of Mr. Shibata was staged!

129
00:08:28,966 --> 00:08:32,345
Mrs. Shimoyama, can you talk to me?

130
00:08:39,143 --> 00:08:45,733
SCHOOL ROUTE
ITABASHI WARD

131
00:08:47,109 --> 00:08:48,528
Goodbye.

132
00:08:51,072 --> 00:08:52,740
-Hello.
-Be careful!

133
00:08:52,823 --> 00:08:55,576
-I'm here to see the principal.
-Go ahead.

134
00:09:00,998 --> 00:09:03,709
CONGRATULATIONS SOCCER TEAM!
TOURNAMENT PARTICIPANTS

135
00:09:08,673 --> 00:09:11,133
Mr. Uramawashi, why are you here?

136
00:09:11,217 --> 00:09:14,762
If you get caught,
I'll be held responsible!

137
00:09:14,845 --> 00:09:17,181
The Tacoma Narrows Bridge
in Washington State

138
00:09:17,265 --> 00:09:21,143
was built without sufficient testing,
and so, after only four months,

139
00:09:22,436 --> 00:09:23,604
it collapsed.

140
00:09:25,106 --> 00:09:27,900
I have no idea what you're talking about,
but please wait.

141
00:09:27,984 --> 00:09:30,152
Please wait!

142
00:09:30,236 --> 00:09:32,446
Are you a rabbit?

143
00:09:32,530 --> 00:09:35,783
Listen, you must not use lies.

144
00:09:35,866 --> 00:09:38,160
I will fight fair and square and win.

145
00:09:38,244 --> 00:09:40,913
I'll store the lies away in the basement.

146
00:09:42,582 --> 00:09:43,916
Thank you for today.

147
00:09:44,000 --> 00:09:45,459
Thank you for coming.

148
00:09:46,252 --> 00:09:49,797
That person over there
is Assembly Member Miku Nijima, right?

149
00:09:49,880 --> 00:09:51,757
If I recall, she’s a former idol…

150
00:09:51,841 --> 00:09:56,262
From Pastel Sugar!
I loved them back when I was a kid!

151
00:09:56,345 --> 00:09:58,681
I’m going to use the restroom.
Go on ahead.

152
00:09:58,764 --> 00:09:59,807
What?

153
00:10:02,518 --> 00:10:04,395
He's in his own world.

154
00:10:05,062 --> 00:10:08,566
That is strictly
Mr. Shibata’s personal issue.

155
00:10:09,317 --> 00:10:13,321
Please don't make it a problem
with our school's management system.

156
00:10:14,196 --> 00:10:19,702
Mr. Shibata had recently been
actively opposing the school merger.

157
00:10:21,120 --> 00:10:23,497
It seems he had been
building up a lot of stress.

158
00:10:23,581 --> 00:10:25,374
He was opposing a merger?

159
00:10:25,458 --> 00:10:27,960
Was he having trouble
with anyone because of that?

160
00:10:28,044 --> 00:10:31,422
No, nothing comes to mind, but…

161
00:10:32,632 --> 00:10:35,217
Representative Nijima
was also here for the merger?

162
00:10:35,301 --> 00:10:38,971
Yes, we asked her here for her opinions.

163
00:10:40,514 --> 00:10:44,685
Excuse me. I would like to ask you
about this video of Sho Shimoyama.

164
00:10:44,769 --> 00:10:46,395
I don't know anything about it.

165
00:10:46,479 --> 00:10:48,397
-Let's go.
-Yeah.

166
00:10:49,148 --> 00:10:52,902
-What was she asking you about?
-About the video.

167
00:10:57,031 --> 00:10:59,700
School merger, huh?

168
00:11:02,411 --> 00:11:03,913
Wait, where did he go?

169
00:11:05,122 --> 00:11:07,124
MR. URAMAWASHI
MEET ME AT CLASS 3-1

170
00:11:10,670 --> 00:11:14,423
Geez! What are you doing…

171
00:11:14,507 --> 00:11:19,470
Let me introduce you to the person
who filmed our viral video.

172
00:11:19,553 --> 00:11:21,597
Taiga Takanashi.

173
00:11:22,681 --> 00:11:25,017
How did you know it was him?

174
00:11:25,101 --> 00:11:27,770
I guessed the filming location
from the video’s angle,

175
00:11:28,646 --> 00:11:30,272
and it led to his seat.

176
00:11:32,108 --> 00:11:34,985
Takanashi is the ace of the soccer team,

177
00:11:35,069 --> 00:11:39,323
so everyone was too scared
of him to speak up.

178
00:11:40,324 --> 00:11:41,158
Am I right?

179
00:11:45,871 --> 00:11:48,332
Would you mind telling us about it?

180
00:11:49,333 --> 00:11:52,420
It's nothing much.
I just filmed Sho by accident.

181
00:11:52,503 --> 00:11:54,463
But you set up your camera in advance.

182
00:11:54,547 --> 00:11:56,257
I did no such thing.

183
00:11:57,049 --> 00:11:58,551
If you don't mind,

184
00:11:59,802 --> 00:12:04,306
I would like to see the video.

185
00:12:24,160 --> 00:12:25,661
Are you okay?

186
00:12:26,412 --> 00:12:27,913
Hold on!

187
00:12:34,795 --> 00:12:36,255
Stop!

188
00:12:37,256 --> 00:12:38,883
I'm sorry, are you okay?

189
00:12:39,800 --> 00:12:41,844
Wait for me!

190
00:12:50,769 --> 00:12:52,021
How?

191
00:12:52,104 --> 00:12:57,985
Know the layout of the school building,
and you can predict the escape routes.

192
00:12:58,068 --> 00:12:59,445
Mr. Uramawashi?!

193
00:12:59,528 --> 00:13:01,489
How did you beat me here?

194
00:13:03,115 --> 00:13:05,159
Don't be so on guard.

195
00:13:05,868 --> 00:13:07,411
You forgot something.

196
00:13:08,204 --> 00:13:09,872
I just want to return it to you.

197
00:13:10,456 --> 00:13:12,750
-My phone!
-When you bumped into me…

198
00:13:12,833 --> 00:13:15,085
You dropped it…

199
00:13:24,345 --> 00:13:27,806
In the end, we couldn't
get anything out of Mr. Takanashi.

200
00:13:27,890 --> 00:13:33,187
Well then, shall we take a look
at the original video he recorded?

201
00:13:33,270 --> 00:13:35,189
You have the video?

202
00:13:36,023 --> 00:13:38,901
I went through his phone's data
before returning it.

203
00:13:38,984 --> 00:13:41,529
Is that even legal?

204
00:13:48,452 --> 00:13:51,664
So it's because he was smoking.

205
00:13:51,747 --> 00:13:55,251
If a student is found smoking,
it may affect his prospects.

206
00:13:55,334 --> 00:13:59,505
So Mr. Shibata lied and said
it was just about messy clothes.

207
00:13:59,588 --> 00:14:01,382
Do you think lying here is wrong?

208
00:14:03,884 --> 00:14:06,554
Underage smoking is against the law.

209
00:14:06,637 --> 00:14:10,266
Even middle schoolers must be responsible.

210
00:14:11,267 --> 00:14:16,564
So, where do you think
underage smokers usually smoke?

211
00:14:16,647 --> 00:14:18,232
I guess…

212
00:14:18,315 --> 00:14:19,567
Behind the gymnasium.

213
00:14:20,609 --> 00:14:25,656
You're right. But in the video,
he is smoking out in the open!

214
00:14:27,366 --> 00:14:30,703
Come to think of it,
I got a call from my son Taiga earlier.

215
00:14:30,786 --> 00:14:33,831
He said a young lawyer
came to question him.

216
00:14:33,914 --> 00:14:36,959
-That must be Ms. Aso.
-Bingo!

217
00:14:37,042 --> 00:14:39,003
What about the video?
It hasn't been found out yet?

218
00:14:39,086 --> 00:14:42,131
-He said he didn't tell her anything.
-Then it's fine.

219
00:14:42,214 --> 00:14:46,635
If the school merger goes through,
it will be your achievement, Ms. Nijima.

220
00:14:46,719 --> 00:14:50,931
Yes. Otherwise,
we'll have a problem, Mr. Hyuga.

221
00:14:52,016 --> 00:14:56,937
Please make sure you choose
my company to be your contractor,

222
00:14:57,021 --> 00:14:58,147
Mr. Takanashi.

223
00:14:58,230 --> 00:15:03,527
Of course.
Do well, and we'll reward you richly.

224
00:15:07,156 --> 00:15:09,033
It's just as you said, Ms. Aso.

225
00:15:10,034 --> 00:15:13,537
When I searched the house,
I found the signatures.

226
00:15:22,421 --> 00:15:24,089
SIGNATURES AGAINST THE SCHOOL MERGER

227
00:15:24,173 --> 00:15:26,717
He got so many people to sign.

228
00:15:27,927 --> 00:15:29,053
But…

229
00:15:29,803 --> 00:15:31,513
With my father arrested,

230
00:15:32,139 --> 00:15:35,851
it seems the opposition
has been greatly weakened.

231
00:15:35,935 --> 00:15:37,186
Really?

232
00:15:38,896 --> 00:15:41,732
They say they can't side
with a violent teacher.

233
00:15:43,359 --> 00:15:45,903
But my father isn't that kind of person…

234
00:15:48,948 --> 00:15:51,200
I’ll look into it as well.

235
00:15:55,579 --> 00:15:59,625
Regarding Nijima, who Mr. Uramawashi
spotted at Karasawa Junior High,

236
00:15:59,708 --> 00:16:01,627
I checked her social media.

237
00:16:02,628 --> 00:16:04,046
She's a huge fan of Monaki!

238
00:16:04,129 --> 00:16:05,756
That's irrelevant!

239
00:16:05,839 --> 00:16:10,678
She was accused online of having affairs,
and having done nothing of note.

240
00:16:10,761 --> 00:16:14,723
So she wants to push for the school merger
and win some votes.

241
00:16:14,807 --> 00:16:16,600
-Hey, show the next one.
-Okay.

242
00:16:17,434 --> 00:16:20,312
The father of Taiga Takanashi,
who shot the video,

243
00:16:20,396 --> 00:16:22,731
is the CEO
of a major construction company.

244
00:16:22,815 --> 00:16:28,028
Public works projects offer good money,
so he wouldn't want the merger to fail.

245
00:16:28,112 --> 00:16:31,865
However, it seems the real goal
isn't just the school merger.

246
00:16:31,949 --> 00:16:32,783
Huh?

247
00:16:33,409 --> 00:16:35,494
The redevelopment plan for Itabashi Ward.

248
00:16:35,577 --> 00:16:38,747
The land adjacent to Karasawa Junior High
is also in that area.

249
00:16:38,831 --> 00:16:40,958
If they become the main developers,

250
00:16:41,041 --> 00:16:44,086
they can make a lot more money
than just tearing down a school.

251
00:16:44,169 --> 00:16:47,256
So, they framed Mr. Shibata for this?

252
00:16:47,339 --> 00:16:51,635
He was leading the opposition,
but still, he's just a teacher.

253
00:16:52,845 --> 00:16:55,139
-Sorry, I’m late.
-Habu, you!

254
00:16:55,222 --> 00:16:59,226
-I told you to be here at four!
-Unlike you, I was actually working.

255
00:16:59,935 --> 00:17:01,103
-Here.
-Okay.

256
00:17:01,186 --> 00:17:02,813
Show us what you got!

257
00:17:03,605 --> 00:17:07,735
Ms. Manami handed the opposition
signatures Mr. Shibata collected

258
00:17:08,318 --> 00:17:09,737
over to Ms. Aso.

259
00:17:09,820 --> 00:17:12,698
-Did you photograph the signature file?
-Of course I did.

260
00:17:15,576 --> 00:17:16,952
-Not bad.
-Next slide.

261
00:17:18,287 --> 00:17:20,414
Oh, sorry.

262
00:17:22,541 --> 00:17:26,795
I was adjusting the focus.

263
00:17:30,340 --> 00:17:32,634
You only took photos of Ms. Aso!

264
00:17:37,931 --> 00:17:40,851
-This is the file.
-Don't try to play it off!

265
00:17:40,934 --> 00:17:42,978
A direct demand petition.

266
00:17:43,062 --> 00:17:45,981
This would force the assembly
to discuss the issue, right?

267
00:17:46,065 --> 00:17:51,945
And Nijima didn't want it submitted,
so she tried to get rid of Mr. Shibata?

268
00:17:52,029 --> 00:17:54,740
To destroy the opposition's main pillar.

269
00:17:54,823 --> 00:17:58,786
But an ex-idol representative,
and a company CEO?

270
00:17:58,869 --> 00:18:00,412
Isn't this too elaborate?

271
00:18:00,496 --> 00:18:03,040
Perhaps there's a hidden mastermind?

272
00:18:03,582 --> 00:18:05,751
Maybe this lawyer.

273
00:18:05,834 --> 00:18:06,960
ATSUMU HYUGA

274
00:18:07,044 --> 00:18:07,920
His lies.

275
00:18:08,962 --> 00:18:10,297
I'll expose them.

276
00:18:12,049 --> 00:18:15,469
Mr. Uramawashi has not been
up to any problematic behavior so far.

277
00:18:15,552 --> 00:18:17,846
What do you mean
by "problematic behavior"?

278
00:18:17,930 --> 00:18:19,264
For example…

279
00:18:25,104 --> 00:18:29,358
He hasn't been doing any investigations
or contacting any clients on his own.

280
00:18:29,441 --> 00:18:31,652
I see. Not "on his own."

281
00:18:32,319 --> 00:18:33,821
Also, actually,

282
00:18:33,904 --> 00:18:39,034
I took on a new case from a client
I met at Mr. Uramawashi's office.

283
00:18:43,539 --> 00:18:45,165
There's no problem with that.

284
00:18:46,875 --> 00:18:48,252
Thank you.

285
00:18:50,379 --> 00:18:53,882
It's okay. I'm okay…

286
00:18:53,966 --> 00:18:56,927
I wasn't lying.

287
00:18:57,010 --> 00:18:59,471
He didn't do
any of those things "on his own"!

288
00:18:59,555 --> 00:19:02,766
That's right, I didn't lie.

289
00:19:02,850 --> 00:19:04,852
So you two are working together?

290
00:19:04,935 --> 00:19:08,981
As part of my supervision, I need
to keep him within sight. Nothing more.

291
00:19:09,064 --> 00:19:11,525
Part of your supervision, I see.

292
00:19:11,608 --> 00:19:14,361
Did you take on another troublesome case?

293
00:19:14,444 --> 00:19:17,364
A middle school teacher ended up
using violence on a student.

294
00:19:17,447 --> 00:19:18,907
Corporal punishment.

295
00:19:19,700 --> 00:19:22,244
Prohibited under Education Code,
Article 11.

296
00:19:22,327 --> 00:19:24,121
This is clearly an assault case.

297
00:19:24,204 --> 00:19:26,498
I would like to reach
a settlement somehow,

298
00:19:26,582 --> 00:19:29,126
but the merger is complicating things.

299
00:19:29,209 --> 00:19:31,795
With a school merger,

300
00:19:31,879 --> 00:19:34,381
you would think teachers and parents
would end up on the same side.

301
00:19:34,464 --> 00:19:35,841
The same side?

302
00:19:35,924 --> 00:19:40,345
I mean, the school being torn down
would normally be something no one wants.

303
00:20:34,149 --> 00:20:35,275
STUDENT ROSTER

304
00:20:57,881 --> 00:21:02,135
Time to overwrite this blueprint of lies.

305
00:21:09,643 --> 00:21:11,103
Good morning.

306
00:21:11,186 --> 00:21:14,231
Morning Ms. Aso.
Mr. Uramawashi is sleeping.

307
00:21:14,314 --> 00:21:17,317
-Sleeping?
-He pulled an all-nighter.

308
00:21:18,026 --> 00:21:19,194
Must be nice.

309
00:21:19,278 --> 00:21:21,780
I pulled an all-nighter too.
I'm so sleepy.

310
00:21:22,447 --> 00:21:24,700
Then why don't you try using this?

311
00:21:25,701 --> 00:21:26,743
An eye mask?

312
00:21:26,827 --> 00:21:29,413
Yeah, my recommendation.
It's new, so don't worry.

313
00:21:29,496 --> 00:21:31,331
Thank you very much.

314
00:21:34,626 --> 00:21:36,295
-I'm turning it on.
-Okay.

315
00:21:36,878 --> 00:21:38,088
There.

316
00:21:39,423 --> 00:21:43,552
Oh, this feels pretty nice.

317
00:21:44,469 --> 00:21:48,015
Right? A lawyer's body
is their main asset, after all.

318
00:21:48,098 --> 00:21:49,808
SIGNATURES AGAINST THE SCHOOL MERGER

319
00:21:49,891 --> 00:21:54,521
I don't deny democracy itself.

320
00:21:55,314 --> 00:21:57,274
<i>However, in Japan,</i>

321
00:21:57,357 --> 00:22:01,528
<i>obtaining everyone's consensus</i>
<i>takes a lot of time.</i>

322
00:22:01,611 --> 00:22:06,033
<i>And the world will have moved on</i>
<i>to the next stage.</i>

323
00:22:06,116 --> 00:22:08,118
<i>What I want to say is…</i>

324
00:22:08,910 --> 00:22:13,165
<i>What this country needs right now</i>
<i>is speedy decision-making.</i>

325
00:22:13,248 --> 00:22:16,501
Furuse is as popular as ever, huh.

326
00:22:16,585 --> 00:22:22,215
His stance is a bit forceful,
but it's what Japan needs right now.

327
00:22:22,299 --> 00:22:24,760
He makes you nervous in person.

328
00:22:24,843 --> 00:22:26,386
His presence is intense.

329
00:22:27,220 --> 00:22:30,891
And all I did was greet him
at a party meeting!

330
00:22:31,641 --> 00:22:34,936
If we score an achievement
and get close to him,

331
00:22:35,020 --> 00:22:37,397
soon we'll be in national politics.

332
00:22:40,192 --> 00:22:43,528
Excuse me.
You have a call from a Mr. Imai.

333
00:22:43,612 --> 00:22:47,032
Imai? I don't know anyone
by that name, though.

334
00:22:47,115 --> 00:22:49,951
They said it's about
the opposition to the school merger.

335
00:22:50,035 --> 00:22:53,622
WHAT DOES JAPANESE POLITICS NEED?

336
00:22:57,417 --> 00:23:01,171
Hello! Nijima speaking.

337
00:23:01,254 --> 00:23:04,132
<i>Mr. Furuse, will you carry that role?</i>

338
00:23:04,216 --> 00:23:06,927
<i>If the citizens desire it,</i>

339
00:23:07,010 --> 00:23:09,513
<i>I am prepared</i>
<i>to carry that responsibility.</i>

340
00:23:10,013 --> 00:23:15,602
<i>Of course, there is pushback</i>
<i>to any reform. Criticism too.</i>

341
00:23:15,685 --> 00:23:18,563
<i>However, because we feared criticism</i>

342
00:23:18,647 --> 00:23:23,360
<i>and kept postponing decisions,</i>
<i>Japan ended up where it is today.</i>

343
00:23:28,490 --> 00:23:32,244
What are you here to talk about?

344
00:23:32,327 --> 00:23:33,745
Well…

345
00:23:33,829 --> 00:23:36,665
Because of the recent violent incident,

346
00:23:36,748 --> 00:23:40,043
some residents are more drawn
to supporting the merger.

347
00:23:40,710 --> 00:23:42,462
The ones who used to oppose it?

348
00:23:43,463 --> 00:23:47,509
However, there are still
many residents on the fence,

349
00:23:47,592 --> 00:23:51,429
so if we provide the venue,
can you host an informational meeting?

350
00:23:51,513 --> 00:23:53,890
An explanatory meeting?

351
00:23:53,974 --> 00:23:56,268
Yes, they just need one final push.

352
00:23:56,351 --> 00:23:58,645
Is that story really true?

353
00:23:59,354 --> 00:24:01,982
Do you mean I'm lying?

354
00:24:02,649 --> 00:24:08,321
Maybe you plan to stall us by making us do
a meeting where no one intends to listen.

355
00:24:08,405 --> 00:24:10,115
A trap by the opposition?

356
00:24:10,198 --> 00:24:11,950
That's not true.

357
00:24:18,748 --> 00:24:21,334
Look, I have proof.

358
00:24:21,418 --> 00:24:22,294
SIGNATURES

359
00:24:22,377 --> 00:24:26,381
These are the signatures for the petition
that Mr. Shibata was gathering.

360
00:24:27,174 --> 00:24:28,633
Excuse me.

361
00:24:36,141 --> 00:24:37,434
This doesn't look like…

362
00:24:38,101 --> 00:24:39,769
a copy.

363
00:24:39,853 --> 00:24:41,605
It's definitely the real thing.

364
00:24:44,024 --> 00:24:48,653
If we succeed in persuading
the opposition, even the relocation fees…

365
00:24:52,449 --> 00:24:55,911
Understood.
Let's hold the explanatory meeting.

366
00:24:55,994 --> 00:24:57,495
Thank you very much.

367
00:24:57,579 --> 00:24:58,955
If you'll excuse me.

368
00:24:59,039 --> 00:25:00,582
Wait, please.

369
00:25:00,665 --> 00:25:02,834
Please leave the signatures with me.

370
00:25:02,918 --> 00:25:03,960
What?

371
00:25:04,044 --> 00:25:06,296
If you're leaving the opposition,
it should be no issue.

372
00:25:13,094 --> 00:25:14,137
Okay.

373
00:25:15,430 --> 00:25:17,891
I'll be expecting
the relocation fee, then.

374
00:25:18,600 --> 00:25:20,352
Thank you very much.

375
00:25:23,855 --> 00:25:25,941
You took photos
of all the signatures, right?

376
00:25:26,024 --> 00:25:27,525
<i>Yes, just in case.</i>

377
00:25:27,609 --> 00:25:29,361
Recreate them right now.

378
00:25:29,444 --> 00:25:30,737
<i>Huh? Why?</i>

379
00:25:30,820 --> 00:25:34,282
Please, I'm begging you.
Ms. Aso will kill me.

380
00:25:37,535 --> 00:25:40,205
The opposition was surprisingly stubborn.

381
00:25:40,705 --> 00:25:44,876
There is no way they can gather
enough signatures with just one week left.

382
00:25:46,962 --> 00:25:51,800
BREAK THE HYPOCRITICAL TRIO'S PLAN

383
00:25:53,760 --> 00:25:56,805
This is the schedule
for the three of them.

384
00:25:59,349 --> 00:26:02,227
-There's no day when all three are free.
-What do we do?

385
00:26:02,310 --> 00:26:04,354
Handling them separately is impossible.

386
00:26:04,437 --> 00:26:05,647
What now?

387
00:26:08,316 --> 00:26:09,276
What about here?

388
00:26:09,359 --> 00:26:13,363
I can't make it on this day.
I've also been invited to this wedding.

389
00:26:14,030 --> 00:26:16,533
Hyuga and Nijima…

390
00:26:18,368 --> 00:26:20,120
Should we invite them there?

391
00:26:20,620 --> 00:26:23,790
THE RELATIONSHIP BETWEEN THE THREE

392
00:26:23,873 --> 00:26:25,417
Congratulations.

393
00:26:25,917 --> 00:26:27,919
<i>Next up for our bride and groom</i>

394
00:26:28,003 --> 00:26:32,132
<i>is the wedding cake cutting</i>
<i>and the first bite ceremony!</i>

395
00:26:32,215 --> 00:26:36,261
How's this? It's all about the vibes.
How about we put it here?

396
00:26:36,344 --> 00:26:38,346
What do you think?

397
00:26:39,723 --> 00:26:42,600
Isn't doing an interview at a wedding
a bit implausible?

398
00:26:42,684 --> 00:26:44,227
Stop complaining and look.

399
00:26:44,311 --> 00:26:47,647
There are many people around,
we'll blend in, and no one will notice.

400
00:26:47,731 --> 00:26:49,566
Minori, let me know if he does anything!

401
00:26:49,649 --> 00:26:50,942
I'll give him a kicking!

402
00:26:51,026 --> 00:26:54,779
<i>Everyone, please give them</i>
<i>a big round of applause!</i>

403
00:26:54,863 --> 00:26:57,365
Takanashi can monitor
from right next to them too.

404
00:26:57,449 --> 00:26:58,700
So, what's the situation?

405
00:26:58,783 --> 00:27:01,077
Nijima is almost done with her makeup.

406
00:27:01,661 --> 00:27:03,955
-Right on time.
-Sorry to keep you waiting.

407
00:27:05,206 --> 00:27:08,918
Allow me to guide you
to the interview room. This way.

408
00:27:09,961 --> 00:27:12,839
They are having an outfit change.
Takanashi's heading over.

409
00:27:15,008 --> 00:27:17,510
I'll show you to the waiting room
on the second floor.

410
00:27:20,513 --> 00:27:21,723
<i>Right now?</i>

411
00:27:23,183 --> 00:27:25,560
They're going to cross paths!

412
00:27:27,729 --> 00:27:29,397
Sorry, Ai.

413
00:27:29,481 --> 00:27:32,525
Nijima and Hyuga
already know what I look like.

414
00:27:33,318 --> 00:27:37,155
Huh? Are you Mikurin from Pastel Sugar?
Please shake my hand!

415
00:27:37,238 --> 00:27:39,324
-Hey…
-Sorry, I'm working.

416
00:27:39,407 --> 00:27:43,161
But I'm a huge fan!
Can I at least get a picture?

417
00:27:44,371 --> 00:27:47,332
-Are you a Monaki fan?
-Yes, I am!

418
00:27:47,415 --> 00:27:50,001
Wait, Mikurin, you like Monaki too?

419
00:27:50,085 --> 00:27:51,127
Yes.

420
00:27:52,170 --> 00:27:54,964
Oh, man! Just one picture, please!

421
00:27:55,048 --> 00:27:58,176
-One should be fine.
-Thank you! Over here, please.

422
00:27:58,259 --> 00:28:02,389
I'm so happy right now!
So, who is your favorite?

423
00:28:02,472 --> 00:28:03,515
I like all of them.

424
00:28:03,598 --> 00:28:07,102
-Once ready, the staff will guide you.
-Okay.

425
00:28:07,602 --> 00:28:08,728
Same!

426
00:28:08,812 --> 00:28:12,357
Come on, isn't this schedule
way too tight?

427
00:28:14,943 --> 00:28:18,154
We've been expecting you.
Thank you for your time today.

428
00:28:18,238 --> 00:28:20,115
-Right this way.
-Here.

429
00:28:20,198 --> 00:28:22,242
-The cable!
-Sorry.

430
00:28:24,911 --> 00:28:27,664
-Is here fine?
-Yes, please take a seat.

431
00:28:27,747 --> 00:28:30,834
-We sent you a script…
-I looked at it.

432
00:28:31,459 --> 00:28:33,294
Thank you so much.

433
00:28:34,170 --> 00:28:36,798
Everyone, please be sure to check it out!

434
00:28:37,882 --> 00:28:40,468
Got it! Thank you!

435
00:28:40,552 --> 00:28:44,347
You came out nicely.
You'll be number one, Ms. Nijima.

436
00:28:44,431 --> 00:28:47,225
Well, considering my opposition…

437
00:28:47,308 --> 00:28:49,185
Thank you very much.

438
00:28:49,269 --> 00:28:50,770
-My bag.
-Here.

439
00:28:50,854 --> 00:28:53,356
-Thank you very much.
-This way.

440
00:28:56,151 --> 00:28:58,611
Ms. Nijima is returning
to the waiting room.

441
00:29:00,280 --> 00:29:01,656
Please put this away.

442
00:29:04,826 --> 00:29:07,912
-Good work today!
-Thank you.

443
00:29:07,996 --> 00:29:12,500
-Thank you.
-Hey, what are you doing? Hurry it up.

444
00:29:12,584 --> 00:29:15,503
-I'm sorry. Right this way.
-Yeah.

445
00:29:16,921 --> 00:29:19,799
Wait, I'm not ready yet, hurry!

446
00:29:20,467 --> 00:29:22,343
<i>Hyuga is here!</i>

447
00:29:22,427 --> 00:29:23,553
Hold him off for a sec!

448
00:29:23,636 --> 00:29:27,474
-Mr. Hyuga, we've been waiting for you!
-Oh, hello.

449
00:29:27,557 --> 00:29:30,059
Do you always host interviews
in places like this?

450
00:29:30,143 --> 00:29:33,271
Due to scheduling conflicts,
this was the only venue available…

451
00:29:34,606 --> 00:29:39,027
-Are you thirsty?
-I'm fine. Let's start right away.

452
00:29:39,110 --> 00:29:41,654
-I can't stall him!
-Did you say third floor?

453
00:29:41,738 --> 00:29:43,114
This way, sir.

454
00:29:45,074 --> 00:29:46,993
They're definitely going to cross paths!

455
00:29:47,076 --> 00:29:49,454
-Huh?
-Oh, nothing.

456
00:29:51,706 --> 00:29:54,501
I really wanted to be in this magazine.

457
00:29:54,584 --> 00:29:57,545
I have all the past issues!

458
00:29:58,171 --> 00:30:01,216
Are you Kenji Moriya from Dragon Wash?

459
00:30:01,299 --> 00:30:02,509
No, I'm not.

460
00:30:02,592 --> 00:30:04,302
-What?
-Do I look like him?

461
00:30:04,385 --> 00:30:06,596
You're so cool! You look just like him!

462
00:30:06,679 --> 00:30:10,725
Not hitting on you or anything,
but may I take a picture?

463
00:30:10,809 --> 00:30:12,393
Oh, sure.

464
00:30:12,477 --> 00:30:15,188
Really? Thank you so much! I'm so happy!

465
00:30:15,271 --> 00:30:18,399
<i>Ms. Nijima is heading back too!</i>
<i>Somebody stop her!</i>

466
00:30:22,570 --> 00:30:25,156
Thank you very much.
Please go down these stairs.

467
00:30:25,240 --> 00:30:27,867
-I'm taking the elevator back.
-No, but…

468
00:30:27,951 --> 00:30:30,245
The stairs would be faster!

469
00:30:30,328 --> 00:30:32,664
This elevator is broken.

470
00:30:32,747 --> 00:30:34,249
I think it still works.

471
00:30:39,838 --> 00:30:41,047
After you.

472
00:30:42,590 --> 00:30:44,008
Thank you.

473
00:30:45,051 --> 00:30:47,554
-Goodbye.
-Thank you.

474
00:30:50,807 --> 00:30:54,811
I'm really sorry.
I went to the wrong floor.

475
00:30:54,894 --> 00:30:56,896
May I? Thank you so much!

476
00:30:56,980 --> 00:30:59,190
I'm so happy. Here we go.

477
00:30:59,274 --> 00:31:00,441
Say cheese!

478
00:31:00,525 --> 00:31:04,112
So cool!
Wait, can I take a pic of just you?

479
00:31:04,195 --> 00:31:06,614
Thank you so much.

480
00:31:06,698 --> 00:31:08,116
Oh, wow!

481
00:31:10,910 --> 00:31:13,413
Nice job, everyone!

482
00:31:14,038 --> 00:31:16,165
Thank you very much.

483
00:31:16,249 --> 00:31:19,002
I think our readers
at <i>Modern Wall </i>will be thrilled

484
00:31:19,085 --> 00:31:21,254
to read about your tips
for a good sleep, sir.

485
00:31:21,337 --> 00:31:24,048
Glad to help.
Feel free to invite me again.

486
00:31:24,132 --> 00:31:26,259
-Thank you very much.
-Bye.

487
00:31:32,807 --> 00:31:34,976
Excuse me. I'm Hyuga.

488
00:31:35,059 --> 00:31:37,770
-Please, come on in. Yes!
-Over there?

489
00:31:38,813 --> 00:31:41,608
I'm Harada from <i>Meow's Week</i>.

490
00:31:41,691 --> 00:31:45,653
I would like to ask
about your cat, Mr. Hyuga.

491
00:31:45,737 --> 00:31:47,363
-Nice to meet you.
-Likewise.

492
00:31:47,447 --> 00:31:49,908
-Please have a seat.
-Okay.

493
00:31:51,492 --> 00:31:55,914
-Well then, let's get started.
-Yes, please.

494
00:32:02,045 --> 00:32:04,505
You're Sho Shimoyama, right?

495
00:32:06,007 --> 00:32:09,177
I'm Aso, the lawyer
representing Mr. Shibata.

496
00:32:09,260 --> 00:32:11,054
Do you have some time?

497
00:32:15,391 --> 00:32:19,062
Mr. Shibata never told anyone
that you smoked.

498
00:32:20,438 --> 00:32:25,234
I think he believed you weren't a student
who would do something like that.

499
00:32:27,987 --> 00:32:32,033
Did someone force you to smoke?

500
00:32:34,410 --> 00:32:39,624
-Can we finish this by tomorrow?
-Do we get late-night overtime pay?

501
00:32:41,042 --> 00:32:42,543
No, but Mr. Kureta got us this.

502
00:32:43,127 --> 00:32:45,546
Hold on, sweets?

503
00:32:45,630 --> 00:32:47,757
Pretty sweet deal, right?

504
00:32:49,258 --> 00:32:52,220
Come on, don't say
bad puns with a straight face.

505
00:32:52,303 --> 00:32:57,350
Quit your late-night fooling around.
Get to work!

506
00:32:57,433 --> 00:33:01,145
Come on, do a Monaki dance for us!

507
00:33:01,229 --> 00:33:02,313
Guess I must.

508
00:33:05,108 --> 00:33:06,317
-Anyway, Nakazaki.
-Yeah?

509
00:33:06,401 --> 00:33:10,113
-You got the data from Hyuga's computer?
-I gave it to Mr. Uramawashi.

510
00:33:10,196 --> 00:33:11,739
-Really?
-Hey, look at my dance!

511
00:33:11,823 --> 00:33:15,535
-Show me later. I want to see it.
-Okay.

512
00:33:15,618 --> 00:33:17,412
-Forward it to me.
-Okay.

513
00:33:17,495 --> 00:33:21,165
-Hey, dance, I want to see!
-Do you really?

514
00:33:21,249 --> 00:33:22,625
<i>I want to see!</i>

515
00:33:22,709 --> 00:33:25,086
<i>Then watch this time!</i>

516
00:33:26,921 --> 00:33:28,339
<i>Watch me!</i>

517
00:33:31,968 --> 00:33:36,180
SHIMOYAMA

518
00:33:39,183 --> 00:33:43,521
You again? No matter how many times
you come, nothing will change.

519
00:33:45,898 --> 00:33:47,483
I found this.

520
00:33:51,029 --> 00:33:52,613
SIGNATURES AGAINST THE SCHOOL MERGER

521
00:33:55,408 --> 00:33:56,242
YUKIE SHIMOYAMA

522
00:33:56,325 --> 00:33:57,910
Mrs. Shimoyama,

523
00:33:57,994 --> 00:34:00,830
you were against the school merger
the whole time, weren't you?

524
00:34:04,208 --> 00:34:06,294
What really happened?

525
00:34:08,129 --> 00:34:12,216
I will definitely help you.
Please talk to me.

526
00:34:19,682 --> 00:34:22,852
-We've been expecting you. This way.
-Thank you.

527
00:34:22,935 --> 00:34:26,814
-Thank you for coming.
-Quite a crowd.

528
00:34:26,898 --> 00:34:29,150
-Hello.
-This way.

529
00:34:29,233 --> 00:34:31,819
-Good morning.
-Morning.

530
00:34:34,655 --> 00:34:36,282
Today's materials.

531
00:34:36,365 --> 00:34:38,826
I'll hand them to the person in charge.

532
00:34:40,203 --> 00:34:41,412
Come in.

533
00:34:42,205 --> 00:34:45,041
-Pleasure working with you today.
-Likewise.

534
00:34:45,124 --> 00:34:48,711
I've prepared the script
and video materials right here.

535
00:34:49,545 --> 00:34:52,465
You're a great help.
Preparing materials is a pain.

536
00:34:52,548 --> 00:34:55,134
All that hard work pays off today.

537
00:34:56,135 --> 00:34:58,721
It's all going according
to Mr. Hyuga's plan.

538
00:34:59,555 --> 00:35:01,599
Trusting you was the right choice.

539
00:35:20,868 --> 00:35:22,328
Come in.

540
00:35:22,411 --> 00:35:23,621
Excuse me.

541
00:35:23,704 --> 00:35:27,458
The data you gave me earlier is playing
on the monitor now. Please check.

542
00:35:27,542 --> 00:35:29,168
-Okay.
-Okay.

543
00:35:29,252 --> 00:35:32,296
You keep checking.
I'm going to the restroom.

544
00:35:32,380 --> 00:35:33,631
Okay.

545
00:35:35,299 --> 00:35:37,927
Wait, it won't open!

546
00:35:38,010 --> 00:35:39,428
Let me look at it.

547
00:35:40,429 --> 00:35:41,681
<i>I heard back in your idol days,</i>

548
00:35:41,764 --> 00:35:44,225
<i>you had to sacrifice sleep,</i>
<i>and it was tough.</i>

549
00:35:44,308 --> 00:35:47,687
<i>Yeah. Everyone goes through that, right?</i>

550
00:35:47,770 --> 00:35:52,233
<i>You have a great track record as a leader,</i>
<i>Ms. Nijima.</i>

551
00:35:52,733 --> 00:35:56,654
<i>Of course. If I hadn't taken the lead</i>
<i>and pulled them along,</i>

552
00:35:56,737 --> 00:35:58,698
<i>nothing would have changed.</i>

553
00:35:58,781 --> 00:36:00,199
What is this?

554
00:36:00,283 --> 00:36:04,495
That's some great editing! You did great.

555
00:36:04,579 --> 00:36:06,497
I didn't do anything.

556
00:36:07,707 --> 00:36:11,210
<i>Do you think Takanashi Construction</i>
<i>can survive moving forward?</i>

557
00:36:11,294 --> 00:36:14,797
<i>If they don't adapt with the times,</i>
<i>they're just going to vanish.</i>

558
00:36:15,840 --> 00:36:17,925
This isn't what I was asked!

559
00:36:18,593 --> 00:36:23,014
<i>It's kind of embarrassing</i>
<i>to see them cling to outdated ways.</i>

560
00:36:23,097 --> 00:36:24,724
What is the meaning of this?

561
00:36:25,516 --> 00:36:27,476
It was just a magazine interview, I was…

562
00:36:27,560 --> 00:36:29,270
Don't play dumb!

563
00:36:29,353 --> 00:36:31,647
The question is about
Takanashi Construction!

564
00:36:31,731 --> 00:36:33,149
And you said you hate them!

565
00:36:33,232 --> 00:36:34,483
-Is that so?
-I didn't!

566
00:36:34,567 --> 00:36:35,693
Huh, that's me?

567
00:36:35,776 --> 00:36:39,071
<i>What's your take on the allegations</i>
<i>that Nijima is having affairs?</i>

568
00:36:39,155 --> 00:36:40,740
<i>She's for sure doing it.</i>

569
00:36:40,823 --> 00:36:43,743
<i>I can tell who has</i>
<i>by looking in their eyes.</i>

570
00:36:43,826 --> 00:36:46,787
-Wait, what is this?
<i>-So she won despite cheating?</i>

571
00:36:48,623 --> 00:36:51,042
<i>Well, you know, pillow talk is important.</i>

572
00:36:51,125 --> 00:36:53,544
<i>You mean Ms. Nijima slept around</i>
<i>to get promotions?</i>

573
00:36:53,628 --> 00:36:54,420
<i>That's right.</i>

574
00:36:55,004 --> 00:36:57,506
<i>The one who sleeps well wins.</i>

575
00:36:57,590 --> 00:36:59,300
No, come on…

576
00:36:59,383 --> 00:37:02,345
Is that what you think of me?

577
00:37:02,428 --> 00:37:05,640
<i>-I don't like that stuff.</i>
-Don't mess with me!

578
00:37:05,723 --> 00:37:10,228
<i>Well, I wouldn't mind trying, though.</i>
<i>I could get hooked.</i>

579
00:37:10,728 --> 00:37:14,023
I got it! I was talking
about secrets to good health!

580
00:37:14,106 --> 00:37:14,941
That hurts!

581
00:37:15,024 --> 00:37:18,569
You. What's the deal with this video?
Did you betray me?

582
00:37:18,653 --> 00:37:22,573
I don't know! I only handed
the materials for the meeting!

583
00:37:22,657 --> 00:37:24,909
I just plugged in the USB drive
I was given!

584
00:37:24,992 --> 00:37:27,787
-Then what about this…
-Just delete it!

585
00:37:27,870 --> 00:37:29,497
Delete it right now!

586
00:37:30,122 --> 00:37:33,876
<i>Were Ms. Nijima and President Takanashi</i>
<i>easy to handle?</i>

587
00:37:33,960 --> 00:37:38,965
<i>Yes. Dangle some bait in front of them,</i>
<i>and they'll do as you say.</i>

588
00:37:39,048 --> 00:37:42,093
<i>If so, does it mean they're not smart?</i>

589
00:37:42,176 --> 00:37:46,347
<i>Basically, they're incapable of</i>
<i>understanding anything complicated.</i>

590
00:37:49,308 --> 00:37:51,435
<i>They're good kids and really cute</i>

591
00:37:51,519 --> 00:37:54,272
<i>when they're eating</i>
<i>out of the palm of my hand.</i>

592
00:37:54,355 --> 00:37:55,690
Don't get violent.

593
00:37:55,773 --> 00:37:59,568
-I was talking about my cat.
-You were looking down on me, bastard!

594
00:37:59,652 --> 00:38:01,320
How dare you make a fool out of me?

595
00:38:01,404 --> 00:38:05,825
Hey, if I weren't here,
you guys wouldn't be able to do anything!

596
00:38:05,908 --> 00:38:06,909
You mock me!

597
00:38:06,993 --> 00:38:09,829
<i>She is so simple-minded,</i>
<i>it's kind of cute!</i>

598
00:38:09,912 --> 00:38:13,624
You airheaded idol-turned-politician!
Don't get cocky!

599
00:38:13,708 --> 00:38:16,127
And you exploit your employees
to line your own pockets!

600
00:38:16,711 --> 00:38:21,173
I'm fed up with how stupid you two are!

601
00:38:21,257 --> 00:38:24,010
Assembly Members
shouldn't be on reality shows!

602
00:38:24,093 --> 00:38:27,305
Assembly Members have freedom too!

603
00:38:39,233 --> 00:38:42,111
Dad! What are you doing?

604
00:38:46,282 --> 00:38:49,452
Everyone, this video is a fake!

605
00:38:49,535 --> 00:38:51,579
It's all fabricated!

606
00:38:51,662 --> 00:38:55,207
Yes. Fake videos like these
are so easy to make!

607
00:38:56,208 --> 00:39:02,506
That abusive teacher, Shibata,
pulled strings to frame us!

608
00:39:02,590 --> 00:39:04,300
That's not true!

609
00:39:04,383 --> 00:39:07,011
My dad would never do
anything so cowardly!

610
00:39:07,678 --> 00:39:10,306
Even if he got violent,
there had to be a reason for it!

611
00:39:10,890 --> 00:39:14,643
You're his daughter.
Whatever you say is useless.

612
00:39:14,727 --> 00:39:19,648
The evidence of his violence
still remains in the video!

613
00:39:19,732 --> 00:39:23,903
-Well, there are videos of you guys too!
-Yeah!

614
00:39:23,986 --> 00:39:27,823
I told you, this is all fake!

615
00:39:28,491 --> 00:39:30,201
We can say that too!

616
00:39:34,872 --> 00:39:37,041
Mr. Shibata is the victim here!

617
00:39:37,124 --> 00:39:41,420
That video
was intentionally filmed to frame him!

618
00:39:42,213 --> 00:39:43,506
Mom…

619
00:39:43,589 --> 00:39:46,384
It's true, right?

620
00:39:49,303 --> 00:39:50,763
My son…

621
00:39:51,680 --> 00:39:55,017
Because I'm frail and can't work,

622
00:39:55,768 --> 00:40:01,399
he accepted money to pretend to smoke
in front of Mr. Shibata.

623
00:40:03,401 --> 00:40:05,986
But the fact remains
that he hit him, right?

624
00:40:06,654 --> 00:40:07,696
Right?

625
00:40:17,665 --> 00:40:18,874
Sho…

626
00:40:21,001 --> 00:40:24,839
It's meaningless
to obtain things through lies.

627
00:40:32,221 --> 00:40:34,140
-He didn't hit me.
-Sho!

628
00:40:34,223 --> 00:40:35,933
I don't want to lie anymore!

629
00:40:40,855 --> 00:40:46,277
Mr. Shibata just took away the cigarette,
and I pretended to be hit and fell over.

630
00:40:47,111 --> 00:40:48,988
The bruise I had back then

631
00:40:49,947 --> 00:40:52,533
was because Taiga hit me.

632
00:40:59,123 --> 00:41:02,376
I am truly, deeply sorry.

633
00:41:03,836 --> 00:41:07,298
I will apologize to Mr. Shibata too.

634
00:41:08,340 --> 00:41:12,344
I am so sorry.

635
00:41:36,035 --> 00:41:37,244
You…

636
00:41:37,328 --> 00:41:38,412
You were the one

637
00:41:38,496 --> 00:41:42,750
who advised President Takanashi
and Ms. Nijima on this plan.

638
00:41:46,962 --> 00:41:49,215
What?

639
00:41:50,257 --> 00:41:53,469
Where is your proof?

640
00:41:57,806 --> 00:41:58,641
What?

641
00:42:00,851 --> 00:42:03,187
What a pain in the ass.

642
00:42:03,270 --> 00:42:04,688
ITABASHI WARD REDEVELOPMENT BID

643
00:42:04,772 --> 00:42:09,902
I have records of you commissioning
the fake video and paying for it,

644
00:42:10,611 --> 00:42:12,363
along with other proof of your corruption.

645
00:42:13,656 --> 00:42:15,991
How did you get your hands on this?

646
00:42:18,452 --> 00:42:23,332
You probably used
illegal means again, didn't you?

647
00:42:24,375 --> 00:42:28,170
In the end, you're nothing
more than that murderer's--

648
00:42:31,966 --> 00:42:34,677
Careless words invite ruin.

649
00:42:37,221 --> 00:42:40,015
I'll make sure you never defend again.

650
00:42:45,813 --> 00:42:48,023
You'd better watch your mouth.

651
00:42:54,446 --> 00:42:56,865
Murderer?

652
00:43:02,580 --> 00:43:05,457
After the incident, Ms. Nijima resigned.

653
00:43:05,541 --> 00:43:08,711
Takanashi Construction is also pulling out
of the public works projects.

654
00:43:09,587 --> 00:43:11,005
Great job out there.

655
00:43:13,424 --> 00:43:19,138
By the way, just to confirm,
Mr. Uramawashi wasn't involved, right?

656
00:43:29,523 --> 00:43:31,609
I'm sorry. Please don't ask.

657
00:43:31,692 --> 00:43:33,986
That's pretty much an answer right there.

658
00:43:34,528 --> 00:43:37,573
SUPER VIRAL WATCH

659
00:43:37,656 --> 00:43:39,325
The likes keep going up!

660
00:43:39,408 --> 00:43:44,288
-True.
-Our late-night editing was worth it.

661
00:43:44,371 --> 00:43:48,375
-Let's make a video of you next.
-Stop it!

662
00:43:48,459 --> 00:43:50,961
-Don't do it.
-Boss.

663
00:43:51,045 --> 00:43:53,047
The receipts I promised you.

664
00:43:53,130 --> 00:43:55,883
Damn it, I thought I was going to win!

665
00:43:55,966 --> 00:43:57,426
What's this?

666
00:43:57,509 --> 00:43:59,970
We had a bet on whether
Ms. Aso would make it in time.

667
00:44:00,054 --> 00:44:01,472
Excuse me!

668
00:44:02,181 --> 00:44:05,017
Ms. Aso, good morning.

669
00:44:07,519 --> 00:44:13,317
I had a hunch you were scheming something.
Why didn't you tell me?

670
00:44:13,859 --> 00:44:18,781
You can't tell a lie.
You would have told them everything.

671
00:44:20,366 --> 00:44:24,912
But you said you stored
the lies away in the basement!

672
00:44:26,538 --> 00:44:29,458
My house is single-story.

673
00:44:29,541 --> 00:44:30,959
What?

674
00:44:31,919 --> 00:44:35,422
This is why I hate lies.

675
00:44:36,465 --> 00:44:38,425
I'm grateful to you, Aso.

676
00:44:38,509 --> 00:44:39,343
Huh?

677
00:44:40,052 --> 00:44:43,472
You brought Sho Shimoyama's
mother to the school.

678
00:44:45,891 --> 00:44:48,811
Keep doing your best without lying.

679
00:44:49,520 --> 00:44:52,314
No need to tell me.

680
00:44:52,398 --> 00:44:56,026
Also, it looks like the school merger
will be scrapped.

681
00:44:56,110 --> 00:44:59,530
-The violence charge will be dropped too.
-A moment, Mr. Uramawashi?

682
00:45:06,995 --> 00:45:09,164
Sorry!

683
00:45:12,376 --> 00:45:13,585
What?

684
00:45:19,466 --> 00:45:21,760
JUSTICE'S FORM

685
00:45:23,429 --> 00:45:24,471
LEARN THE LAW, BUT DOUBT IT

686
00:45:26,390 --> 00:45:30,477
THE LAW ISN'T ALWAYS RIGHT
FIND YOUR OWN JUSTICE

687
00:45:32,146 --> 00:45:34,815
MIYUKI SHIRAMOTO
BORN 1981, KANAGAWA

688
00:45:46,535 --> 00:45:47,911
<i>Nice to meet you, woof!</i>

689
00:45:49,746 --> 00:45:51,540
You must remain silent.

690
00:45:52,207 --> 00:45:55,085
<i>They had Public Security plant evidence?</i>

691
00:45:56,211 --> 00:45:57,880
<i>We'll remake the lie.</i>

692
00:45:57,963 --> 00:46:01,633
-Hey!
<i>-Intruders detected.</i>

693
00:46:02,217 --> 00:46:07,097
Shall I show you
the moment your lies crumble?

694
00:46:07,181 --> 00:46:08,140
Subtitle translation by: Nix S.
